  "notes": [
    "Modbus RTU over RS485 (terminals 10 +, 11 -, 12 shield). Address 1 to 255; 9600 to 115200 bit/s; even, odd or no parity; response delay 0 to 200 ms. The settings are in the Comunicação menu (C.adr, C.brt, C.pary, C.deLy); the manual gives no factory values.",
    "The manual lists the registers as 40001 on with an offset column from 0; the map uses the offset, as sent on the wire. The mnemonic column of the manual's table is partly shifted against the descriptions, so the order of the descriptions and the register numbers named in the bit-mask tables (status 40002 to 40004, relay command 40007, baud rate 40009, parity 40010, input type 40012, retransmission 40075 to 40077) decide.",
    "Values are signed 16-bit integers; the displayed and engineering values use the decimal places in register 17. The manual does not give the scaling of the ambient temperature or the analog output value.",
    "Bit 0 of the general status (calibration memory fault) is marked as not implemented in the manual.",
    "Written from the manufacturer's manual; not tested on a device."
  ],
  "protocol": "rtu",
  "unit_id": 1,
  "databits": 8,
  "byte_order": "big",
  "word_order": "big",
  "address_base": 0,
  "x_status": "official",
